\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God the All- terrible! King, 
\par who ordainest
\par Great winds Thy clarions, 
\par the lightnings Thy sword;
\par Show forth Thy pity on high 
\par where Thou reignest;
\par Give to us peace in our time, 
\par O Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. God the All- merciful! 
\par Earth hath forsaken
\par Thy way of blessedness, 
\par slighted Thy word;
\par Bid not Thy wrath in its 
\par terrors awaken;
\par Give to us peace in our time,
\par O Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God the All- righteous One! 
\par Man hath defied Thee;
\par Yet to eternity 
\par standeth Thy word;
\par Falsehood and wrong shall not 
\par tarry beside Thee;
\par Give to us peace in our time, 
\par O Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. God the All- wise! 
\par By the fire of Thy chastening,
\par Earth shall to freedom and 
\par truth be restored;
\par Through the thick darkness 
\par Thy kingdom is hastening;
\par Thou wilt give peace in Thy time,
\par O Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So shall Thy children 
\par in thankful devotion
\par Laud Him who saved them 
\par from peril abhorred,
\par Singing in chorus from 
\par ocean to ocean:
\par Peace to the nations and praise 
\par to the Lord.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

